    "updated_at": "2020-04-20T16:56:20Z",
    "body": "We've had several proposals to do async or post-facto rendering in the prompt in the past (e.g. rendering most of the prompt to allow interactive usage, but then letting slow modules like Java or git-status populate in the prompt afterwards).\r\n\r\nThe big blocker in every single attempt to do this has been that one of our big draws is cross-platform and cross-shell uniformity, so anything we do needs to be supported across many shells, and (as far as I know, though admittedly I don't know much), each shell has its own async rendering API.\r\n\r\nIf we can somehow unify these pieces into a single internal API (perhaps using the `STARSHIP_SHELL` environmental variable and some more clever hackery in our initialization scripts), then we could potentially unlock a lot of really cool pieces, but I think this would have to wait until at least the completion of format strings. However, I'd love to see this done, if it's possible!",
